  "question": {
    "text": "Mark the correct order of decreasing acid strength of the following compounds. <br/><img src=\"assets\\qt0033_e44cb8307f96.png\" style=\"width:4.68333in;height:1.225in\">"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "(V) &gt; (IV) &gt; (II) &gt; (I) &gt; (III)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "(II) &gt; (IV) &gt; (I) &gt; (III) &gt; (V)",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "(IV) &gt; (V) &gt; (III) &gt; (II) &gt; (I)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "(V) &gt; (IV) &gt; (III) &gt; (II) &gt; (I)",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "The electron withdrawing group <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> increases the acidity of phenols and the electron donating group <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> decreases the acidity of phenols. The effect oat p-position is greater than at m-position. <br/>Hence the order of acidic nature is (II) &gt; (IV) &gt; (I) &gt; (III) &gt; (V)."
  }
